{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/163370-ritemasters","id":163370,"title":"Ritemasters","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-09T04:13:00-07:00","id":163370,"title":"Ritemasters","content":"So some might disagree some might agree but I always wanted to play a ritemaster but always felt useless. Most of the rites didn't just feel niche they felt that they could easily be replicated by normal abilities. I was wondering if they would get a boost for the idigam chronicles so could keep up with other characters albeit in different ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T05:03:05-07:00","id":163403,"title":"","content":"The spoiler on rites isn't likely to pop up until Friday, possibly later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T05:12:45-07:00","id":163413,"title":"","content":"To quote Acrozatarim in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161194-idigam-weekly-discussion-storm-lords-bones-of-ice\">the Storm Lords thread</a>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161194-idigam-weekly-discussion-storm-lords-bones-of-ice?p=161232#post161232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, FOR NO REASON WHATSOEVER, is it ok if I throw out a request into this thread for opinions about Rites? Any thoughts from people about bits or elements of the old Rites systems that you really liked or hated? Not just the stuff in the corebook, but were there any particular developments in how Rites were handled in later books that you thought were good or need to be steered away from?<br /> <br /> Just... assessing opinions.<br /> <br /> No reason. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Similarly, <i>for no reason whatsoever</i>, I'd suggest catching his eye and discussing what you want from Rites, particularly regarding how ritemaster characters could be made more awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T05:15:17-07:00","id":163437,"title":"","content":"You'll have the spoilers this Friday if I work hard enough during the week <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> My brief opinion on rites: The current list has a lot of chaff in it, plenty of which doesn't even mechanically need to be a rite at all. Then there's stuff like the Rite of Dedication which is widely hated with a passion. It doesn't feel enough like drawing on ancient spirit pacts and bans, even though that's what rites are supposed to be. And, of course, we've changed how Harmony works so you can expect the old rite system to be changing in turn (I always hated ritemasters having to use their Harmony for rites, it made sod all sense).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T05:23:46-07:00","id":163445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/163370-ritemasters?p=163437#post163437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'll have the spoilers this Friday if I work hard enough during the week <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> My brief opinion on rites: The current list has a lot of chaff in it, plenty of which doesn't even mechanically need to be a rite at all. Then there's stuff like the Rite of Dedication which is widely hated with a passion. It doesn't feel enough like drawing on ancient spirit pacts and bans, even though that's what rites are supposed to be. And, of course, we've changed how Harmony works so you can expect the old rite system to be changing in turn (I always hated ritemasters having to use their Harmony for rites, it made sod all sense).</div> </div> </div> </div>That'll be nice to see. Personally, i wouldn't mind rites that required Primal Urge+Attribute or more rites required Essence or health levels to be used to fuel the rites. Harmony while really annoying didn't bug me as much as just there being this area that was thematically interesting but not worth it to focus on. Some of them felt really out of of place like Rite of Dedication and The Binding of Locks. The idea that prey can't escape makes sense. That you would do it in the form of locking every door not so much. Considering how many ways spirits can ignore that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 06-09-2014, 08:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T05:44:53-07:00","id":163455,"title":"","content":"There's two things to note about Binding of Locks:<br /> - Remember that rites draw on spiritual power, they aren't <i>just</i> for using against spirits. Spirits might have ways round locked doors but lots of other prey don't.<br /> - Ethan Skemp had this excellent notion about using rites to change the environs into horror-movie style situations. The series of rites that Binding of Locks was part of are an exploration down that path of thinking. That said, and as some may have noticed from the Gift Facets that Stew revealed on the blog a few weeks back, I've actually gone and put a lot of that theme into certain Gifts now. You can expect that the core Rites list will probably not go down that particular path. Can't say anything for sure at this stage, of course - first draft and all that!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T09:45:04-07:00","id":163694,"title":"","content":"Binding of Locks is pretty much the absolute <i>perfect </i>example of what a rite should be like - the whole &quot;turning environment into horror movie settings&quot; is the best thing about rites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T12:37:52-07:00","id":163909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/163370-ritemasters?p=163455#post163455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's two things to note about Binding of Locks:<br /> - Remember that rites draw on spiritual power, they aren't <i>just</i> for using against spirits. Spirits might have ways round locked doors but lots of other prey don't.<br /> - Ethan Skemp had this excellent notion about using rites to change the environs into horror-movie style situations. The series of rites that Binding of Locks was part of are an exploration down that path of thinking. That said, and as some may have noticed from the Gift Facets that Stew revealed on the blog a few weeks back, I've actually gone and put a lot of that theme into certain Gifts now. You can expect that the core Rites list will probably not go down that particular path. Can't say anything for sure at this stage, of course - first draft and all that!</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true. However, the way it works. Wouldn't it be easier to prevent a prey from leaving an area? In a sense a more survival horror of silent hill rather than something out of Halloween? To be honest, I don't think that it's an issue of a power I just think Four dots for it seems off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T13:21:10-07:00","id":163949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/163370-ritemasters?p=163909#post163909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's true. However, the way it works. Wouldn't it be easier to prevent a prey from leaving an area? In a sense a more survival horror of silent hill rather than something out of Halloween? To be honest, I don't think that it's an issue of a power I just think Four dots for it seems off.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you think Rites like Call Human and Bind Human are for? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> However, Bind Human <i>requires </i>that they leave at least one means of escape and that could be one reason for Binding the Locks to be a 4 dot Rite. The 2 dot Rite of Bind Human requires a loop hole, which is why it's less powerful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T13:48:47-07:00","id":163968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/163370-ritemasters?p=163949#post163949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What do you think Rites like Call Human and Bind Human are for? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> However, Bind Human <i>requires </i>that they leave at least one means of escape and that could be one reason for Binding the Locks to be a 4 dot Rite. The 2 dot Rite of Bind Human requires a loop hole, which is why it's less powerful.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you were already in your car though it doesn't stop you from just driving away. Especially with the length it takes for the ritual to go on. I'm really just hoping that for the time and effort most of them get better for their exp cost and effort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T14:44:39-07:00","id":164043,"title":"","content":"Well, that's why you do the Bind Human and Binding the Locks first, <i>then </i>Call Human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T14:57:46-07:00","id":164064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/163370-ritemasters?p=164043#post164043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, that's why you do the Bind Human and Binding the Locks first, <i>then </i>Call Human.</div> </div> </div> </div>...That seems like a lot of work when some normal dice and the right tools will do the same thing in just about the same amount of time. I guess if you didn't know where the person was but there just seems faster ways to find them than setting something like this up. I mean with the right tracking gifts it seems unnecessary. It's not like binding of locks will change anything or bind human. Just use Call human and use superior strength to win. I mean unless you get some kind of kick out of doing something like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T15:00:04-07:00","id":164068,"title":"","content":"I'm reminded of the wild orgiastic and demonic rituals from Howling 2: Your Sister is a Werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T15:17:10-07:00","id":164084,"title":"","content":"Maybe, but it's not as much <b>FUN!</b> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> And, y'know, there's that part about how you can perform these Rites on a Spirit-Ridden, which may not be as easy to overpower, so you want all the advantages you can get.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T15:27:22-07:00","id":164091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/163370-ritemasters?p=163455#post163455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Ethan Skemp had this excellent notion about using rites to change the environs into horror-movie style situations. The series of rites that Binding of Locks was part of are an exploration down that path of thinking</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this from the Rage book? Where's Ethan Skemp's idea elaborated upon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T16:39:56-07:00","id":164194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/163370-ritemasters?p=163437#post163437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'll have the spoilers this Friday if I work hard enough during the week <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Then there's stuff like the Rite of Dedication which is widely hated with a passion.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, if it is still possible to contribute to the feel of Rites in IC, while I have no mechanical suggestions, I definitely hope the feel of a ritualmaster is part shaman, part wiseman, and part &quot;don't mess with him since otherwise you will regret it.&quot; Currently, Rites have no real feel of power to them, despite having some very powerful effects. As it stands, most of the ritual preparation in my games was simply glossed over since nobody wanted to hear yet again how the Ithaeur was drawing yet another binding circle, then performing another summoning ritual, then performing the sacred hunt rite, etc. It was more tedious than anything.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T19:37:06-07:00","id":164314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/163370-ritemasters?p=163455#post163455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's two things to note about Binding of Locks:<br /> - Remember that rites draw on spiritual power, they aren't <i>just</i> for using against spirits. Spirits might have ways round locked doors but lots of other prey don't.<br /> - Ethan Skemp had this excellent notion about using rites to change the environs into horror-movie style situations. The series of rites that Binding of Locks was part of are an exploration down that path of thinking. That said, and as some may have noticed from the Gift Facets that Stew revealed on the blog a few weeks back, I've actually gone and put a lot of that theme into certain Gifts now. You can expect that the core Rites list will probably not go down that particular path. Can't say anything for sure at this stage, of course - first draft and all that!</div> </div> </div> </div>Some rites need to be explicitly more useful. Let's take Bind Spirit, for example. Can a spirit bound Blast outside the circle? (I lean at 'no'; but it's never stated what being bound entails beyond restricted mobility, or how that allows you to have spirits carry on errands for you, once they're not bound again) can I use it like a ward with the specific ban on spirits? No, it only works for an specific one. This is a rank 3 rite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T19:52:11-07:00","id":164325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/163370-ritemasters?p=164043#post164043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, that's why you do the Bind Human and Binding the Locks first, <i>then </i>Call Human.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great, I now keep picturing a ritemaster getting angry with an Iron Master because he pulled out a cellphone to call the person they are trying to get to come.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T19:53:44-07:00","id":164328,"title":"","content":"Whoa, wait a second. Since when was Rite of Dedication widely hated? I was under the impression that it was one of the most useful Rites. Why is it hated?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T20:32:27-07:00","id":164356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahuman101</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/163370-ritemasters?p=164328#post164328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whoa, wait a second. Since when was Rite of Dedication widely hated? I was under the impression that it was one of the most useful Rites. Why is it hated?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it's lame that you have to have a rite to do something that should be automatic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T20:57:00-07:00","id":164392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/163370-ritemasters?p=164356#post164356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because it's lame that you have to have a rite to do something that should be automatic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, I don't understand. How should it be &quot;automatic&quot;? Taking items into the Shadow, I can understand. But what about the part where your worn items change with you and don't get destroyed? Like, I don't know, YOUR CLOTHES! Are you telling me that this part should be automatic too? Because that make no sense whatsoever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":427,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","user":"Rahuman101","date":". 06-09-2014, 11:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T21:47:19-07:00","id":164472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahuman101</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/163370-ritemasters?p=164392#post164392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sorry, I don't understand. How should it be &quot;automatic&quot;? Taking items into the Shadow, I can understand. But what about the part where your worn items change with you and don't get destroyed? Like, I don't know, YOUR CLOTHES! Are you telling me that this part should be automatic too? Because that make no sense whatsoever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither option makes much sense to me.<br /> <br /> Hulking out of your clothes should be something that happens when you have no idea what you're doing, like First Change, but having to go through a rite to not do it seems overkill. FWC seems to be going in the direction of new tiers of powers for this kind of thing (Mage Sight become an attainment of some kind rather than a full-on spell, for instance); I think something along those lines would work for the Rite of Dedication, too.<br /> <br /> Or you lose anything undedicated if you full-out kuruth, but normally it's fine, your clothes being part of your Hishu form and its purpose, or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T22:02:07-07:00","id":164481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/163370-ritemasters?p=164472#post164472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neither option makes much sense to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves primarily enter the Shadow by phase-shifting themselves through loci rather than hopping over Verges that transform everything that goes through into spiritual ephemera. Pathfinding allows you to bring other conscious entities across the Gauntlet with you, but otherwise the basic means of otherworldly transportation available to the People are those that evoke a more primal degree of viable equipment, and the chief means of mitigating this is a basic ritual (in a culture where basic rituals tend to be fairly commonplace) that also doubles metaphysically as a means of altering your spiritual body-template to save your personal effects from the clash between the basic laws of material physics and your flagrant defiance thereof.<br /> <br /> I don't disagree that it could be handled better mechanically, but I look with overt disdain on any claim that it doesn't <i>make sense</i> and I'll warn you right now that that's an argument that I'm not going to put up with from anybody.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T22:22:22-07:00","id":164516,"title":"","content":"Condition: Nekkid<br /> You didn't just take off your clothes, you ruined them while shapeshifting into gauru, urshul or urhan without wearing dedicated clothes.<br /> Trouble here. The obvious route is a decent penalty with social interaction, and Dexterity. But I could see a bonus to social stuff, as well, depending upon the scene.<br /> The police are likely to be notified.<br /> Beat: The character experiences difficulties that could have been avoided by wearing clothes. (max of one?)<br /> Resolution: The character puts on some clothes. Resolving this condition does not gain a beat.<br /> <br /> Would this promote rampant nudism?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T22:25:46-07:00","id":164518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/163370-ritemasters?p=164516#post164516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would this promote rampant nudism?</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering waking up naked blood soaked is a icon of Werewolf fiction, I say run with it.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T22:26:13-07:00","id":164519,"title":"","content":"Too Sexy For My Shirt<br /> Your character has a very McConaugheyan quality that leaves him unable or at least unwilling to keep a shirt on for any significant amount of time. Any time you roll an exceptional success on an action unrelated to the current status of your character\u2019s shirt, in a scene where a character has paid attention or taken notice of your character\u2019s good looks, you can choose to take this Condition. With this Condition, take a -3 to all Mental actions, since he\u2019s clouded with tension. <br /> Example Skills:Academics, Drive, Empathy<br /> Resolution:Your character removes his shirt. Gain +2 to your next Social action, and your next Physical action.<br /> Beat:N/A","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T22:41:00-07:00","id":164527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/163370-ritemasters?p=164518#post164518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering waking up naked blood soaked is a icon of Werewolf fiction, I say run with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm normally against the 'it happened in this one movie/legend/book' argument, but I don't think I've seen one where a change occurs without clothes being torn to shreds. I suppose the big problem would be who wants to RP running around naked until you get home all the time? Walking home naked after the Siskur-Dah would be rather anticlimactic. Perhaps automatic dedication during the sacred hunt? Let your downtime death rages leave you in the lurch? Of course, if you have a practical mind and can work magic, that would be an early hurdle to overcome, considering werewolves have always walked alongside 'normies.' Which is probably why the rite of dedication exists in the first place. I guess the argument would be that the rites existence forces the ritemaster to get it, lest everyone lose all their belongings all the time. <br /> <br /> Generally when an ability is considered absolutely necessary, as in all groups -must- have it, people tend to think it shouldn't be something someone has to buy, that it should be an innate ability or otherwise free.<br /> <br /> \u200bDo werewolves have a derogatory term for humans? Seems like they should.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T22:48:45-07:00","id":164533,"title":"","content":"Running around naked isn't that much of an issue if you look like a dog. Put a collar on yourself and you're set!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/163370-ritemasters?p=164527#post164527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bDo werewolves have a derogatory term for humans? Seems like they should.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kibble? Hogs? Lunch?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T23:06:26-07:00","id":164540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/163370-ritemasters?p=164533#post164533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Running around naked isn't that much of an issue if you look like a dog. Put a collar on yourself and you're set!</div> </div> </div> </div>Luna's addendum to the Oath of the Moon: The Sacred Prey Must Be Taken Near Pet Supermarket. Bring A Gift Card.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T23:13:45-07:00","id":164546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/163370-ritemasters?p=164540#post164540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Luna's addendum to the Oath of the Moon: The Sacred Prey Must Be Taken Near Pet Supermarket. Bring A Gift Card.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I can just picture a pack with one pretending to be a disabled guy while the other runs around as his &quot;helper dog&quot;. Allows for easy recon of buildings.<br /> <br /> Hell, they could probably rob the store while there at it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T04:41:10-07:00","id":164706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/163370-ritemasters?p=163694#post163694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Binding of Locks is pretty much the absolute <i>perfect </i>example of what a rite should be like - the whole &quot;turning environment into horror movie settings&quot; is the best thing about rites.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would normally agree, but I've already moved it more into the province of Gifts in IC (for example, there's an upgraded version of Binding of Locks that's now a Facet).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T04:42:33-07:00","id":164707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/163370-ritemasters?p=164091#post164091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is this from the Rage book? Where's Ethan Skemp's idea elaborated upon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't currently get from where I'm sat to my pile of Werewolf books to check due to a rampaging baby who would just love an unattended laptop to poke the keyboard of, but yes, I think it's in the rage, the 'Hunting' rites in there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T04:46:29-07:00","id":164708,"title":"","content":"Rite of Dedication was an example of an 'admin' rite, and one that existed purely to patch a hole. It did so via adding an additional bit of bean-counting to the system (how many Dedicated items can I have/do I currently have?), was essentially a mandatory rite that your Ithaeur had to take or else everyone was constantly running to the charity shops to buy some cheap new clothes, and didn't really add anything to the game.<br /> <br /> The area of the game that Dedication used to cover has been folded into another element of the IC mechanics and is both a) far simpler and b) doesn't require an admin rite that someone has to take.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T04:55:31-07:00","id":164730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/163370-ritemasters?p=164194#post164194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, if it is still possible to contribute to the feel of Rites in IC, while I have no mechanical suggestions, I definitely hope the feel of a ritualmaster is part shaman, part wiseman, and part &quot;don't mess with him since otherwise you will regret it.&quot; Currently, Rites have no real feel of power to them, despite having some very powerful effects. As it stands, most of the ritual preparation in my games was simply glossed over since nobody wanted to hear yet again how the Ithaeur was drawing yet another binding circle, then performing another summoning ritual, then performing the sacred hunt rite, etc. It was more tedious than anything.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How to make the preparation and performance of a ritual more relevant to the game is one of the task's we're looking to tackle in IC.<br /> <br /> For example, in our playtest session last night, DaveB was playing the Bone Shadow Ithaeur attempting a rite. He came up with an initial version of how to perform it, then realised that mechanically the impact of the performance he had chosen was... less than optimal. Since the rite was occurring right at the end of the session, we ended it there, and DaveB is now considering carefully how to change the rite performance for the beginning of next session to better fit his ithaeur's strengths and benefit from the accompanying mechanical element of rite use.<br /> <br /> Tl;dr: New system should give the performance of a rite mechanical impact.<br /> <br /> Addendum to the above: Currently based on not-even-full-first-draft of Rites, cannot guarantee this teaser will match final product, product may have sprouted wings, turned green or exploded, etc etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T10:04:51-07:00","id":164907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/163370-ritemasters?p=164527#post164527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bDo werewolves have a derogatory term for humans? Seems like they should.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sheep? I may have read too much DRC, where they constantly refer to clothes as &quot;sheepskin&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=78